tely reproduced (not \"fixed\")\n- **siphash sign-extension bug**: `data = d[0]|…|(d[3]<<24)` is an `int`, so `d[3] ≥ 0x80` sign-extends and floods the upper 32 bits — this is why lengths 4–7 hash identically. Same for `case 4:` in the tail switch.\n- **seed is a no-op** in `hash_bytes` (`^ seed` applied twice cancels).\n- `temp_key` is *not* updated when an existing string key is found in the wrapped half of a bucket.\n- `arrgrowf(NULL, es, 0, 0)` returns `NULL`; `arrfreef(NULL)` frees `NULL-32`; `hash_index.temp_key` is left uninitialized by `make_hash_index`.\n- `str_dups`' `printf(\"%s %d\\n\", strmap[z], strmap[z].value)` passes a 16-byte struct to a varargs `%s`/`%d`; per the SysV AMD64 ABI the two eightbytes land in the first two vararg registers, so it prints `key` then `value` — reproduced by passing `(key, value, value)`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":362,"cache_read_input_tokens":155428,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":362,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"34f58a0a-1270-4871-9648-c35728ff0f03","uuid":"76e06283-6c20-4ff8-a01a-e5025901229f","timestamp":"2026-08-20T05:17:57.590Z"}
